# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Reference material — not part of the build
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A BARE / AGAIN AS OF 2026-08-30. This was "assets/insperation_pictures/*" plus a
# negation for the .gdignore inside it -- the trailing /* was load-bearing, because
# git never looks inside an excluded directory to check per-file negations. The
# project owner deleted the directory along with the retired UI packs, so there is
# no longer a file in there to un-ignore and the gotcha no longer applies.
assets/insperation_pictures/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RETIRED 2026-08-30 — the Kibyra itch.io UI packs.
#
# This block used to list each pack's directory and NEGATE the README and the
# two .url links, because a developer had to download the packs by hand or the
# game had no HUD. asset_request.md [P8] replaced every piece of that art with
# the project's own, so nothing in the repo points here any more: the README,
# the .url files and the local copies under game/assets/ui/ are all gone, and
# game/assets/LICENCES.md's "not shipped" rows for them went with them.
#
# THE WHOLE DIRECTORY IS IGNORED NOW RATHER THAN UNIGNORED, and that is the
# point of the change: the packs are still on developers' disks (mine has ~1500
# files in there) and lifting the rules would make git offer to commit all of
# them — which is the redistribution the old rules existed to prevent. So the
# constraint has not gone away, it has stopped being anybody's problem.
#
# THE DIRECTORY IS NOW GONE FROM THE OWNER'S DISK TOO (2026-08-30), and this rule
# STAYS anyway. It costs nothing and it is the guard for the one thing that would
# undo the retirement: a developer re-downloading the packs to look at the old art
# and git cheerfully offering to commit all ~1500 files.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
assets/UI_Sprites/

# HUD icon source sheets (game/assets/LICENCES.md) -- the project owner's own
# Gemini-generated working sheets, kept locally so the 5x5 sheet's remaining
# empty slots can be filled from the same artwork, but not needed in the repo.
assets/Icons/

# Loose Gemini working-source drops at the assets/ root (e.g. MainMenu.png,
# Age_and_Upgrade_bar.png) -- same convention as assets/Icons/ above: the cut
# asset actually used ships from game/assets/ui/, the raw source stays local.
# Not recursive, so a real subfolder (UI_Sprites/, Icons/) is unaffected.
assets/*.png
assets/*.jpg

# Raw art source (0 A.D. checkout, Blender working files).
# Lives outside the repo entirely — see PLAN.md §1.3
art_source/
art_work/

